## 3x3 center tile mirrored into a 9x9 grid (task-d729ce84)
When a 3x3 input is expanded to 9x9, copy it into the central 3x3 region and mirror it across the center tile's edges: the adjacent top/bottom tiles are vertical reflections; the adjacent left/right tiles are horizontal reflections; the four corner tiles are reflected in both axes (180-degree rotation). Equivalently, map each output row and column index through `f=[2,1,0,0,1,2,2,1,0]` and set `output[r][c]=input[f[r]][f[c]]` for 0<=r,c<9. This exactly reproduced the demo and solved test for task-d729ce84. Demo input `[[7,6,7],[2,7,6],[1,2,7]]` output is the 9x9 mirrored expansion; test `[[8,8,6],[6,3,6],[6,8,8]]` solved with same rule. The demo's corner blocks happened to equal the input transpose because that demo input was symmetric under half-turn; use the reflection-coordinate formula rather than inferring a transpose rule.
